<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Clonard Abbey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Clonard Abbey was a monastery in County Meath, Ireland, founded by Finnian of Clonard in the early 6th century. It became one of the great schools of early Irish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>, and tradition makes its founder the teacher of the 'Twelve Apostles of Ireland', including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a>. It was later a bishopric and an Augustinian house, of which little survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/clonard-abbey.jpg" alt="Clonard Abbey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andreas F. Borchert · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clonard_Monastic_Site_Anglican_Church_2007_08_26.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
